From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:37:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sdk, dll: return interface structs the way MSVC's member
 functions do

An MSVC-built game calls an interface method that returns a struct
(CSteamID, SteamIPAddress_t, the controller action data) with the result's
address after this and reads that address back from RAX. A MinGW build
returns an 8-byte struct in RAX instead, and the SDK's MinGW declarations
(STEAMWORKS_STRUCT_RETURN) return void: either way the game dereferences
garbage. En Garde! (Unreal Engine 5.1) faulted reading address
0x011000010c1bb449, its own Steam ID, right after ISteamUser::GetSteamID.

Every struct-returning pure virtual in sdk/steam now goes through
STEAMWORKS_STRUCT_RETURN, whose MinGW form takes the result first and
returns a reference to it (the MSVC layout), and each implementation
provides that overload.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-30-en-garde.md
Offered-upstream: no
